# Hyperlink everything

When you mention anything that has a canonical URL or location, make it a clickable link instead of plain text. This covers PRs, issues, commits, branches, files and line ranges, CLI commands and tools, docs, and any sources you cite.

- Use the identifier itself as link text: [#123](url), [ENG-456](url), [`src/auth.ts:42`](url).
- For code, prefer permalinks pinned to a commit SHA, or a local file path with line number when working locally.
- Link CLI commands and tools to their official docs on first mention.
- Link each identifier on first mention only; repeat mentions can stay plain.
- Never guess or fabricate URLs. If you can't resolve the real link, leave it unlinked.
